---------------------------------------------------------------------
I. SYSTEM OVERVIEW
---------------------------------------------------------------------
text‑to‑cad is a modular, skill‑based CAD/robotics/fabrication engine
that converts NATURAL LANGUAGE or IMAGES into:

  • CAD solids (STEP, STL, 3MF, GLB)
  • DXF 2D profiles
  • URDF robot models
  • SRDF planning configs
  • SDF simulation worlds
  • G‑code for FDM printers
  • DfAM printability analysis
  • Off‑the‑shelf STEP part retrieval
  • Implicit CAD (SDF‑based geometry)

It acts as a **finite geometric transpiler**:
      TEXT → GEOMETRY → FABRICATION

This aligns directly with RDG finite‑structure modeling:
      SID.Structure → SID.Interaction → SID.Dynamics
      PED.Power → PED.Evaluation → PED.Dynamics

---------------------------------------------------------------------
II. CORE SKILL TYPES
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Each skill is a callable module with its own input/output schema.

1. TYPE: CAD_GENERATION
   INPUT:
     - description: str (plain language)
     - image: bytes (optional)
     - constraints: {dim: float, tol: float, features: [...]}
   OUTPUT:
     - step_model: STEP
     - mesh: STL/3MF/GLB
   FUNDAMENTAL OPS:
     - feature_extraction()
     - parametric_solve()
     - solid_model()
   VARIABLES:
     dim[], tol, feature[], material_tag

2. TYPE: DXF_GENERATION
   INPUT:
     - geometry: polyline[], arc[], spline[]
     - thickness: float
   OUTPUT:
     - dxf_file
   FUNDAMENTALS:
     - 2D projection
     - profile extraction
     - layer tagging
   VARIABLES:
     poly[], arc[], layer_id

3. TYPE: URDF_GENERATION
   INPUT:
     - links: {name, mass, inertia, mesh}
     - joints: {type, parent, child, axis, limits}
   OUTPUT:
     - urdf.xml
   FUNDAMENTALS:
     - kinematic chain assembly
     - inertial tensor mapping
   VARIABLES:
     link[], joint[], inertia[3x3], axis[3]

4. TYPE: SRDF_GENERATION
   INPUT:
     - planning_groups
     - end_effectors
     - collision_rules
   OUTPUT:
     - srdf.xml
   FUNDAMENTALS:
     - group clustering
     - kinematic reachability
   VARIABLES:
     group[], ee[], collision[]

5. TYPE: SDF_GENERATION
   INPUT:
     - world: {frames, lights, sensors, physics}
   OUTPUT:
     - sdf.xml
   FUNDAMENTALS:
     - spatial frame graph
     - rigid body placement
   VARIABLES:
     frame[], sensor[], light[], physics_tag

6. TYPE: STEP_PART_SEARCH
   INPUT:
     - part_name
     - spec: {thread, bearing_size, motor_kv}
   OUTPUT:
     - step_file
   FUNDAMENTALS:
     - catalog lookup
     - parametric filtering
   VARIABLES:
     part_id, spec[]

7. TYPE: DFAM_CHECK
   INPUT:
     - mesh: STL
     - printer_profile
   OUTPUT:
     - report: {overhangs, wall_thickness, supports, orientation}
   FUNDAMENTALS:
     - voxelization
     - local curvature analysis
   VARIABLES:
     voxel[], curvature[], support_vol

8. TYPE: GCODE_SLICE
   INPUT:
     - mesh: STL
     - printer_profile
   OUTPUT:
     - gcode
   FUNDAMENTALS:
     - slicing
     - infill generation
     - extrusion path planning
   VARIABLES:
     layer[], speed, temp, infill_pattern

9. TYPE: BAMBU_LABS_INTEGRATION
   INPUT:
     - gcode
   OUTPUT:
     - job_status
   FUNDAMENTALS:
     - dry_run()
     - upload()
   VARIABLES:
     job_id, printer_state

10. TYPE: IMPLICIT_CAD
    INPUT:
      - sdf_expression: GLSL
    OUTPUT:
      - rendered mesh
    FUNDAMENTALS:
      - signed distance fields
      - raymarch rendering
    VARIABLES:
      sdf(x,y,z), grad[], iso_level

