III. PIPELINE ARCHITECTURE
---------------------------------------------------------------------
text‑to‑cad is structured as a multi‑stage finite pipeline:

  STAGE 1: NATURAL LANGUAGE PARSING
    → extract geometric primitives
    → identify constraints
    → build parametric intent graph

  STAGE 2: GEOMETRIC SYNTHESIS
    → parametric solver
    → feature tree construction
    → solid modeling

  STAGE 3: REPRESENTATION EXPORT
    → STEP (B‑rep)
    → STL/3MF (mesh)
    → DXF (2D)
    → URDF/SRDF/SDF (robotics/simulation)

  STAGE 4: FABRICATION
    → DfAM analysis
    → slicing
    → G‑code generation
    → optional printer upload

This is a **finite relational pipeline**:
      Intent → Structure → Representation → Fabrication

