IV. RDG‑COMPATIBLE MAPPING
---------------------------------------------------------------------
SID (Structure / Interaction / Dynamics)
maps cleanly onto text‑to‑cad:

  SID.Structure:
    - CAD solids
    - DXF profiles
    - URDF link frames
    - SDF world frames

  SID.Interaction:
    - joints
    - constraints
    - collision rules
    - fabrication limits

  SID.Dynamics:
    - robot kinematics
    - simulation physics
    - print path dynamics

PED (Power / Evaluation / Dynamics):

  PED.Power:
    - geometric operators
    - slicing engines
    - SDF solvers

  PED.Evaluation:
    - DfAM checks
    - tolerance validation
    - kinematic reachability

  PED.Dynamics:
    - extrusion path planning
    - robot motion planning
    - simulation time‑stepping

---------------------------------------------------------------------
V. FUNDAMENTAL VARIABLES & OPERATORS
---------------------------------------------------------------------
GEOMETRIC VARIABLES:
  x,y,z           → spatial coordinates
  dim[i]          → dimensions
  tol             → tolerances
  feature[k]      → holes, fillets, chamfers
  mesh[v]         → vertices
  face[f]         → faces
  sdf(x,y,z)      → signed distance field

ROBOTICS VARIABLES:
  link[i]
  joint[j]
  inertia[i][3x3]
  axis[j][3]
  limit[j]

FABRICATION VARIABLES:
  layer[n]
  speed[n]
  temp[n]
  infill[n]
  support_vol

OPERATORS:
  extrude(profile, h)
  revolve(profile, θ)
  fillet(edge, r)
  chamfer(edge, d)
  boolean_union(A,B)
  boolean_subtract(A,B)
  slice(mesh, profile)
  sdf_union(A,B)
  sdf_smooth(A,B,k)

